WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.450
Three kinds of position, three levels of trust.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.325
A DR uses only the course you steered and your speed through the water.

3
00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:10.500
Nothing about current.

4
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.675
Nothing about wind.

5
00:00:12.925 --> 00:00:19.500
An estimated position, an E P, starts with the DR and improves it with whatever else you know.

6
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.425
A known current, say, or a single line of position.

7
00:00:23.675 --> 00:00:25.425
Here’s a neat case.

8
00:00:25.675 --> 00:00:28.675
You have one line of position and a DR.

9
00:00:28.925 --> 00:00:30.750
Where’s your E P?

10
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.700
The point on that line nearest your DR.

11
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:38.650
You know you’re on the line, and that’s the best guess as to where.

12
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.275
A fix is two or more good lines of position at the same time.

13
00:00:43.525 --> 00:00:48.600
So the ranking is: a fix beats an E P, and an E P beats a DR.
